special_phrases.tsv
===================

Source: the OpenStreetMap wiki pages Nominatim/Special_Phrases/EN, /DE, /NL and
/CS (https://wiki.openstreetmap.org/wiki/Nominatim/Special_Phrases), read
through Special:Export on 2026-11-27 at these revisions:

  EN  2861977  2025-06-02T14:00:52Z
  DE  2916988  2025-11-09T11:40:16Z
  NL  2611290  2023-11-03T08:58:05Z
  CS  2052471  2020-10-22T08:16:23Z

Licence: OpenStreetMap wiki content is available under the Creative Commons
Attribution-ShareAlike 2.0 licence (CC BY-SA 2.0,
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0/). The phrases are the work of
the wiki's contributors; see each page's history for the authors.

The file holds the phrases Nominatim imports from those pages with
`nominatim special-phrases --import-from-wiki` and its default settings:

- Every table row with at least five data cells gives (phrase, class, type,
  operator) from its first four. A cell with one single `|` holds attributes
  before it and its content after it, so a row written `| - |Y` has one cell
  fewer and is skipped, as Nominatim's wiki reader skips it.
- Double quotes are removed from the type. An operator other than `in` or
  `near` is `-`.
- Nominatim's default phrase settings drop boundary=administrative and
  place=house/houses, keep only bus_stop, rest_area and raceway' of highway,
  and drop every building phrase. Class and type must each be a single word
  (\w+).
- A repeated (phrase, class, type, operator) is kept once, at its first place.
  The pages are read in the order EN, DE, NL, CS.

12,188 rows read, 9,559 kept. Phrases are not normalised here: the search
normalises them as it does names. Nominatim matches a phrase whatever the
language of the page it came from.

The same rows feed the local Nominatim the search is compared with: written as
CSV (header phrase,class,type,operator), they are what
`nominatim special-phrases --import-from-csv` imports.
